    "text": "My \"one sentence\" check is naive: it flags a period followed by space. Let me look: line 18 is n=?? Let me check which notes. Line 18 and 67 are L8 rows? The check ran on all lines, but the sentence check didn't guard for L8. My regex flagged L8 notes? L8 notes are empty strings — empty note has no \".\" match... unless. Hmm, line 18 = csv row 18 → n=? Let me check the notes at lines 18 and 67. Those are the rejects? No, rejects are lines with n=23 and n=110. Let me print lines 18 and 67.\n\nWait my reduce: lines.map... line index 18 is the 18th line. Let me check.\n\nActually maybe the flagged lines are 23 and 110? The count of lines... index i, \"line \"+(i+1). So line 18 → i=17, n = ? Hmm.\n\nWait, but the rejects were at rows 23 and 110, which would be lines 18 and 67 if 5 rows before 23 are missing from the CSV (n values 8,9,18,20,22 are missing → 23 is the 18th row). Yes! Row order: 1..7 (7 rows), then 10,11,12,13,14,15,16,17 (8 → 15 rows), then 19,21 (→17), then 23 (→18). Yes line 18 = n=23. And 110 at line 67 likely.\n\nSo the \"not one sentence\" flags are my rejects, flagged because my note has \"'Mihai asked for a shared Team lunches calendar'\" containing a \"'.\" ... no, my regex looks for period followed by space. The n=23 note: \"'please add it and make it gold': the coordination gives 'and' three conjuncts and holds 'Mihai asked for a shared Team lunches calendar' as one of them, though no word joins that clause to the command.\" — only one period at the end. Hmm, why flagged? Because the period at end followed by end-of-string? My regex `[^.]\\.(\\s|$)` matches at the end (period followed by end). Oops, my check is broken: it counts the final period. So notes ending with a period get flagged. Both flagged lines are the rejects which end with \".\". Fine — the notes are single sentences.\n\nSo format is OK. Let me double check n=23 and n=110 are indeed lines 18 and 67 to confirm.",
