        "text": "`meetings-07-simple.p01.verdicts.jsonl` is written in this folder: 150 lines, one per CSV row, `n` in the CSV's own order.\n\n**Counts:** 148 × L8, 2 × L3 (n=23, n=110).\n\n**Rejections**\n- n=23, \"'Mihai asked for a shared Team lunches calendar; please add it and make it gold'\" — one coordination with conjunction `and` holds three conjuncts, adding the earlier `asked` clause that no word joins to `add`/`make`. A coordination with a wrong conjunct is L3; the rules fix the anchor as the wire ending right before the conjunction.\n- n=110, \"'please call Ana Annie in the people list'\" — `Ana` and `Annie` are written as one nominal headed by `Annie`, merging the person `call` acts on with the name given to her, the reverse of the allowance for a name after a noun. Two nominals merged is L3.\n\n**What I let pass, and why**\n- Coordinations with no conjunction word (n=56, 95, 105) joining juxtaposed clauses of one message: punctuation puts the clauses side by side and the schema makes `conjunction` optional, so the next layer can continue.\n- Complement vs. modifier choices for bare time phrases (`this week`, `last week`), graded words and words after a measure (`new`, `somewhere quiet`, `teal`, `orange`): the rules exclude what a complement is to its verb and settle the post-nominal adjective as a clause modifier.\n- Relation starts on a nominal rather than the clause, and `attachment=ambiguous` where the words permit either (`in pink`, `with a lime green colour`, `by the lifts`).\n- Split names (`Pod 1`, `Room 301`) as two nominals tied by a markerless relation, and clitic splits (`what's`, `there's`, `doesn't`).\n\nFormat was verified with a local check: all lines parse, keys are exactly `n,grade,note`, `n` matches the CSV row order, and each rejection quotes the message in single quotes. RULES.md refers to `node check.mjs <k>`, but this folder has no `check.mjs`; I did not create one, since the task forbids other files."
      }
